invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: rsa_sign64_power wipes its table and not the entry its last step
  read. That entry is the power the private exponent's last digit names,
  so the dead frame tells four bits of the exponent to whoever reads the
  stack next. No output changes, so no vector notices.
  bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test copies the stack below one call and requires no
  word of any power in the copy.

--- old
    ct_wipe(&table, sizeof table);
    ct_wipe(pick, sizeof pick);
--- new
    ct_wipe(&table, sizeof table);
